","value":201950,"year":"2020 est.","kind":"int"},{"label":"GVA (balanced, total)","value":5039000.0,"year":"2023","kind":"money"},{"label":"GVA per head","value":25304,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":28679,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2715.81,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":2396.07,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"A broadly quiet year at Gateshead: external debt was near-flat at \u00a3670.2m (up \u00a34.3m) against a \u00a3764.7m borrowing need excluding PFI, every prudential indicator was met, and treasury delivered \u00a32.45m of net savings against budget. The council remains \u00a394.5m internally borrowed, and investments fell to \u00a334.8m (from \u00a347.1m) held very short \u2014 an average duration of 2 days including overnight \u2014 while the debt book itself is long-dated, with under 2% of fixed-rate loans maturing within 12 months. The watch item is company lending: a further loan was advanced to the wholly-owned Gateshead Energy Company during the year (after the budget was set), and the council holds Newcastle Airport loan notes which paid deferred interest in 2025/26; neither balance is quantified in this report.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management Annual Report 2025/26","as_of_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49803/TM Annual Report 25-26 Audit Standards Committee.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-14","signals":[{"code":"company-exposure","headline":"Further loan advanced to Gateshead Energy Company in 2025/26 (taken after budget estimates were set); deferred interest received on Newcastle Airport loan notes \u2014 amounts not disclosed in this report","why":"Council cash is committed to owned and part-owned trading companies whose repayments depend on their commercial performance."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a3764.711m excluding PFI (General Fund \u00a3419.206m, HRA \u00a3345.505m; 2024/25 \u00a3754.310m)","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":5},{"name":"borrowing","value":"\u00a3670.182m total external borrowing, a net increase of \u00a34.281m in the year; within the \u00a3836.000m operational borrowing limit","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":4},{"name":"pwlb borrowing","value":"\u00a3622.182m of total borrowing was from the PWLB","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":5},{"name":"investments","value":"\u00a334.814m treasury investments (2024/25: \u00a347.092m); average duration 2 days including overnight, 63 days excluding","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":7},{"name":"internal borrowing","value":"\u00a394.529m (General Fund \u00a357.916m, HRA \u00a336.613m under-borrowing)","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":5},{"name":"treasury outturn vs budget","value":"combined net position \u00a318.690m vs \u00a321.142m budget \u2014 \u00a32.452m net saving (cost of borrowing \u00a323.879m vs \u00a326.597m)","as_at":"2025/26","page":6},{"name":"investment interest","value":"\u00a32.321m earned at average 4.18% (2024/25: \u00a34.442m at 5.19%); \u00a35.189m including third-party and Newcastle Airport loan-note interest, \u00a30.266m below the \u00a35.455m budget","as_at":"2025/26","page":4},{"name":"maturity under 12m","value":"1.74% of fixed-rate borrowing (limit 16%) and 2.39% of variable-rate borrowing (limit 17%) matured within 12 months","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":8}],"commercial":null,"tms_components":null},"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"7.Outturn position 202526 and first quarter review 202627","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49958/7-outturn-position-202526-and-first-quarter-review-202627.pdf","committee":"Tyne and Wear Trading Standards Joint Committee","date":"23/07/2026","key":false},{"title":"RTC - Capital Programme and Prudential Indicators \u2013 Year End Outturn 2025-26 - A","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49893/rtc-capital-programme-and-prudential-indicators-year-end-out.