nd Prudential Indicators \u2013 First Quarter Review 2026-27 - B","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49817/rtc-capital-programme-and-prudential-indicators-first-quarte.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"14/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Revenue Budget \u2013 Provisional Outturn 2025-26 - NK","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49815/revenue-budget-provisional-outturn-2025-26-nk.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"14/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Revenue Budget \u2013 First Quarter Review 2026-27 - NK","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49814/revenue-budget-first-quarter-review-2026-27-nk.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"14/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-26","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49426/annual-governance-statement-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Audit and Standards Committee","date":"23/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Cover report_Treasury Policy and Treasury Strategy","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s48195/cover-report-treasury-policy-and-treasury-strategy.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"19/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"RTC - Treasury Policy Statement and Treasury Strategy 202627 to 203031 A","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s48196/rtc-treasury-policy-statement-and-treasury-strategy-202627-t.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"19/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"RTC - Treasury Policy Statement and Treasury Strategy 202627 to 203031 B","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s48197/rtc-treasury-policy-statement-and-treasury-strategy-202627-t.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"19/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"Report_ Budget","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s48227/report-budget.pdf","committee":"Tyne and Wear Trading Standards Joint Committee","date":"19/03/2026","key":false},{"title":"Appendix 1_Budget","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s48228/appendix-1-budget.pdf","committee":"Tyne and Wear Trading Standards Joint Committee","date":"19/03/2026","key":false},{"title":"RTC - Treasury Policy Statement and Treasury Strategy 202627 to 203031 A","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s48096/rtc-treasury-policy-statement-and-treasury-strategy-202627-t.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"17/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"RTC - Treasury Policy Statement and Treasury Strategy 202627 to 203031 B","url":"https://Gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s48097/rtc-treasury-policy-statement-and-treasury-strategy-202627-t.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"17/03/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[{"title":"Treasury Management Annual Report 2025/26","url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49803/TM Annual Report 25-26 Audit Standards Committee.pdf","committee":"Audit and Standards Committee","date":"2026-07-14","category":"treasury","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","time":"10.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","time":"2.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Housing, Environment and Healthy Communities Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"1.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Care, Health and Wellbeing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"1.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"South Tyne and Wear Waste Management Partnership Joint Executive Committee","time":"1.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-19","committee":"Housing, Environment and Healthy Communities Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"1.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Cabinet","time":"10.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Families Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"4.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-14","committee":"Audit and Standards Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-14","committee":"Cabinet","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Council","time":"2.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Families Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"4.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Corporate Resources Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.gateshead.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Gateshead delivers \u00a32.4m treasury savings but relies on interest rate forecasts","lead":"Gateshead Council generated net treasury savings of \u00a32.452m in 2025/26 through active financial management, achieving a \u00a32.718m underspend on borrowing costs. However, the strategy behind this performance depends on a significant bet. The council deliberately delayed external borrowing and used its own cash reserves instead, banking on Public Works Loan Board interest rates falling in future years. The strategy explicitly carries refinancing risk: if rates do not fall as forecast, the council could face materially higher costs when it eventually borrows to repay those reserves. Internal borrowing stood at \u00a394.529m against investment balances of \u00a334.814m, down 26 per cent from the previous year. The capital financing requirement\u2014the total the council has spent on long-lived assets it has not yet paid for\u2014grew \u00a310.4m to \u00a3764.7m. All prudential indicators remained within approved limits and the Audit and Standards Committee raised no issues.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"KEY - Local Council Tax Support Scheme 202728 A","paper_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50373/50373.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Gateshead's financial surplus masks underlying crisis in adult and children's care spending","lead":"Gateshead Council reported a \u00a38.4m revenue surplus for 2025/26, but the figure masks significant financial strain. A \u00a36.7m one-off dividend from Newcastle International Airport shareholding accounted for most of the surplus; the underlying operational position was far weaker. Adult and Children's Social Care overspent by a combined \u00a36.5m despite the council approving an additional \u00a310.2m in budget for 2026/27, signalling that demand for high-cost placements is outpacing the council's ability to manage costs. The council drew \u00a38.5m from its Budget Sustainability Reserve (the pot of money set aside to bridge to planned savings) in 2025/26 and has budgeted a further \u00a34m draw for 2026/27. A five-year financial plan presented to the committee projects a structural funding gap of \u00a332.5m, and the council acknowledges that \"substantial additional interventions and efficiencies will need to be developed\" beyond the identified social care savings to close it.","iso":"2026-09-21","paper_title":"OSC 2026 Financial Outturn Report - Final","paper_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50355/50355.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"RTC - Treasury Annual Report 202526 A","paper_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50368/50368.pdf","headline":"All prudential indicators within limits; audit committee and internal audit raised no issues","detail":"None of the approved Prudential Indicators for 2025/26 were breached. All debt maturity structures were maintained within agreed upper and lower limits. Audit and Standards Committee reviewed the report on 14 July 2026 with no issues raised. Internal Audit concluded treasury management control systems operating well and all funds safeguarded.","category":"governance","matters":"Good governance and audit clearance provides confidence in financial risk controls and compliance framework","figures":"Zero breaches of Prudential Indicators; all maturity buckets within approved limits","quote":"None of the approved Prudential Indicators set for 2025/26 were breached in the year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"RTC - Treasury Annual Report 202526 A","paper_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50368/50368.pdf","headline":"Capital Financing Requirement increased \u00a310.4m to \u00a3764.7m; external borrowing up \u00a34.3m to \u00a3670.2m","detail":"General Fund CFR increased from \u00a3408.805m to \u00a3419.206m. Total CFR grew from \u00a3754.310m to \u00a3764.711m. External borrowing increased net \u00a34.281m to \u00a3670.182m as \u00a315.0m new borrowing was taken and \u00a310.719m matured. New borrowing was all HRA.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Shows council faces significant ongoing capital financing demands requiring continued external borrowing","figures":"CFR \u00a3764.711m (increase \u00a310.401m); external borrowing \u00a3670.182m (increase \u00a34.281m); new borrowing \u00a315.000m; maturities \u00a310.719m","quote":"The total external borrowing as at 31 March 2026 was \u00a3670.182m, which was within the operational borrowing limit of \u00a3836.000m. This is a net increase of \u00a34.281m from the opening figure of \u00a3665.901m.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"RTC - Treasury Annual Report 202526 A","paper_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50368/50368.pdf","headline":"Council strategy assumes PWLB rates will fall; if wrong, future refinancing costs could be materially higher","detail":"Council deliberately delayed external borrowing to use investment reserves instead, banking on forecast interest rate falls. Council explicitly acknowledges this creates refinancing risk: 'Any short-term savings gained from adopting this approach was weighed against the potential for incurring additional long-term costs by delaying new external borrowing until later years when PWLB long term rates are forecast to be lower.' Internal borrowing stood at \u00a394.529m.","category":"borrowing","matters":"The council is taking strategic interest rate risk; a lender needs to understand this exposure and assess whether the rate forecast is credible","figures":"Internal borrowing \u00a394.529m (\u00a357.916m General Fund, \u00a336.613m HRA); investment balances \u00a334.814m (down 26% from \u00a347.092m prior year)","quote":"Any short-term savings gained from adopting this approach was weighed against the potential for incurring additional long-term costs by delaying new external borrowing until later years when PWLB long term rates are forecast to be lower.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"RTC - Treasury Annual Report 202526 A","paper_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50368/50368.pdf","headline":"Council delivered net treasury savings of \u00a32.452m through active financial management","detail":"Council achieved \u00a32.718m underspend on borrowing costs through strategic use of internal borrowing, partly offset by \u00a30.266m lower investment income. This performance demonstrates effective treasury cost control and day-to-day management.","category":"savings","matters":"Shows the council is managing its treasury actively and controlling borrowing costs effectively despite challenging interest rate environment","figures":"\u00a32.452m net savings; \u00a32.718m borrowing cost underspend; \u00a30.266m investment income shortfall","quote":"Overall Treasury performance against budget for 2025/26 generated net savings of \u00a32.452m","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"RTC - Annual Report of the Audit and Standards Committee 202526 A","paper_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50363/50363.pdf","headline":"External auditor's anticipated opinion on 2024/25 accounts was subject to resolution of matters in relation to pensions.","detail":"The external auditor (Forvis Mazars) anticipated issuing an unqualified opinion on Gateshead's 2024/25 financial statements as of November 2025, but this was conditional on concluding pension-related matters that were then outstanding. The committee annual report does not subsequently report whether these matters were resolved or what the final audit opinion was.","category":"audit","matters":"An audit caveat linked to pension matters signals outstanding issues related to a potentially material liability that would concern a lender assessing financial risk.","figures":"None provided.","quote":"they anticipated issuing an unqualified opinion, without modification, on the financial statements. However, this was subject to the conclusion of matters in relation to pensions.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-22"},"name":"Gateshead","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-22","since_iso":"2026-08-23","distress":false,"headline":"All prudential indicators within limits; audit committee and internal audit raised no issues","lead":"Good governance and audit clearance provides confidence in financial risk controls and compliance framework","also":["19 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-09-22","n_findings":20,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"RTC - Treasury Annual Report 202526 A","top_paper_url":"https://gateshead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50368/50368.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":108,"news_drafts_total":2}}